  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "The test of a pipeline's line asks its form and its one hash on every device and no hit of the driver's.\nThe second pipeline is asked to come from the cache only on a device whose cache keeps pipelines.\nEach pipeline made is said in the log with whether the driver found it in the cache and a hash of its stages' bytes.\nEach package is built at its own version, so its caches keep to a folder of their own, and other versions' folders no run used lately are swept.\nThe pipelines are written to their file on a worker, so the frames go on while the write waits and reads.\nPipelines made on several threads share the driver's cache at once, and the write alone holds it.\nOre turns and walks by fixed steps a frame and says its eye and target, so two runs repeat.\nA probe's ray's hit takes each face of a far glow light as one point at its middle.\nA screen probe no longer marches to a faint glow light that sends it nothing.",
